{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KMUPK5sQAbvVjhr5T12L55","type":"tool_result","content":"OPERATOR QUESTION: As the owner, I want every customer who is sent a code to be readable at the window, so that nobody holding a valid code is turned away. Tonight's measurement says 'Scan from photo' misses roughly 1 code in 7 as designed (1 in 17 with no offer inside), and that the correction level and surface size you signed off on do not change that. Which do you want: (A) land this as built, treat photo-scan as best-effort and rely on the live camera, with [IC-03] dropped and [IC-01]/[IC-02] restated as what is true; (B) put less in the QR — without the campaign id the read rate is ~97%, but the tablet then cannot tie an offline offer to its campaign; (C) fix the scanner's photo decoder first (it is the shipped reader that fails, even on the simplest code), then land this unchanged; or (D) have the server check each code is readable before issuing it and redraw until it is, which needs a decoder on the server that this repo does not have. My recommendation is C, with an attended camera test at the truck before any of them, because the floor is in the reader and not in this card's encoding. ALSO FOR TRIAGE: engineer-level calls made and listed in the merge-intent note for ratification (a long offer line is shortened inside the QR so the symbol never exceeds version 10; media_url is a relative path; the QR's expiry is the UTC date; a second warning identity_not_minted; projections stop after the first failure in one import); out-of-footprint edits stated there (playwright.config.js gains HQ_FF_FIXTURE_PATH so the e2e server can import the committed fixture; routes_test.go's public-surface guard now pins four routes; one status assertion each in subscribers_test.go and marketing-subscribers.spec.js moves from not_sent to minted); a known gap (a code minted but not projected is never re-projected, and pre-existing subscribers get no cod